INSERT INTO public.programme_field_library (field, short_bio, about, study_areas, why_choose, job_market, academic_difficulty, careers) VALUES
('Nursing','Nursing trains you to care for patients, give treatment safely and support people through illness and recovery.','You study how the human body works, common diseases, medicines, and safe patient care. Much of the training happens on the wards, so you learn by practising real clinical skills under supervision alongside classroom work.','{"Anatomy and physiology","Medical-surgical nursing","Pharmacology and drug administration","Maternal and child health","Community health","Clinical practicum"}','Nursing is one of Ghana''s most consistently in-demand qualifications, with clear licensing pathways through the Nursing and Midwifery Council, opportunities in public and private facilities, specialisation options after practice, and qualifications that are often recognised for work abroad.','Ghana Health Service facilities, teaching and regional hospitals, mission and private hospitals, clinics, NGOs and international recruitment. Career paths are broad within health, but tied to the health sector.','High','[{"occupation":"Registered General Nurse","description":"Provides direct patient care in hospitals and clinics.","note":"Requires passing the Nursing and Midwifery Council licensing exam and registration."},{"occupation":"Community Health Nurse","description":"Delivers preventive care, immunisation and health education in communities."},{"occupation":"Nurse Educator","description":"Teaches in nursing training colleges.","note":"Usually needs a degree plus teaching or postgraduate qualification."},{"occupation":"Public Health Officer","description":"Works on disease prevention and health programmes.","note":"Often requires further public health study."},{"occupation":"Nurse Manager","description":"Supervises nursing teams and ward operations.","note":"Requires several years of clinical experience."}]'),
('Midwifery','Midwifery prepares you to care for women during pregnancy, childbirth and after delivery, and to care for newborns.','You learn reproductive anatomy, safe delivery, antenatal and postnatal care, newborn care and emergency obstetric skills. Training is heavily practical, with supervised deliveries and rotations in maternity units.','{"Reproductive anatomy","Antenatal care","Labour and delivery","Newborn care","Obstetric emergencies","Family planning","Clinical practicum"}','Midwives are essential to Ghana''s maternal health goals and are recruited across public, mission and private facilities. The licence is nationally recognised, and experienced midwives can move into specialist practice, teaching or maternal health programme work.','Maternity units, district hospitals, health centres, CHPS compounds, private maternity homes, and maternal health NGOs. Specialised but steady demand nationwide.','High','[{"occupation":"Registered Midwife","description":"Provides antenatal, delivery and postnatal care.","note":"Requires Nursing and Midwifery Council licensing and registration."},{"occupation":"Maternal Health Officer","description":"Supports maternal and child health programmes."},{"occupation":"Midwifery Tutor","description":"Trains student midwives.","note":"Usually needs a degree and teaching qualification."},{"occupation":"Family Planning Counsellor","description":"Advises clients on reproductive health choices."}]'),
('Community Health Nursing','Community health nursing focuses on preventing illness and promoting health in homes, schools and communities rather than mainly in hospitals.','You study public health, immunisation, nutrition, disease surveillance, health education and basic clinical care, with substantial time spent working in communities and CHPS compounds.','{"Community health practice","Immunisation and child welfare","Nutrition","Health promotion and education","Disease surveillance","Basic clinical skills"}','It offers a direct route into Ghana''s primary healthcare system, where community health workers are heavily relied upon, and it opens doors into public health, NGO work and further nursing study.','CHPS compounds, health centres, district health directorates, school health programmes and public health NGOs.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Community Health Nurse","description":"Provides preventive and primary care in communities.","note":"Requires Nursing and Midwifery Council registration."},{"occupation":"Immunisation Officer","description":"Runs child welfare and vaccination services."},{"occupation":"Health Promotion Officer","description":"Designs and delivers community health education."}]'),
('Mental Health Nursing','Mental health nursing trains you to care for people living with mental illness and to support their recovery.','You study psychiatry, psychology, therapeutic communication, medication management and rehabilitation, with clinical placements in psychiatric hospitals and community mental health units.','{"Psychiatric nursing","Psychology and human behaviour","Psychopharmacology","Therapeutic communication","Community mental health","Clinical practicum"}','Mental health is an under-served area in Ghana with growing national attention, so trained specialists are scarce and valued, with pathways into community mental health, counselling and further study.','Psychiatric hospitals, general hospital psychiatric units, community mental health teams, rehabilitation centres and mental health NGOs.','High','[{"occupation":"Registered Mental Health Nurse","description":"Cares for patients with mental health conditions.","note":"Requires Nursing and Midwifery Council registration."},{"occupation":"Community Mental Health Officer","description":"Follows up patients and families in the community."},{"occupation":"Rehabilitation Support Worker","description":"Supports recovery and reintegration programmes."}]'),
('Critical Care Nursing','Critical care nursing is post-basic training for nurses caring for seriously ill patients in intensive care units.','Building on general nursing, you study advanced physiology, life support, ventilation, monitoring equipment and emergency management, with intensive supervised ICU practice.','{"Advanced physiology","Life support and resuscitation","Ventilation and airway management","Haemodynamic monitoring","Critical care pharmacology","ICU practicum"}','It is a specialist qualification that increases responsibility and employability in tertiary hospitals, and is often required for ICU posts locally and abroad.','Teaching hospitals, regional hospital ICUs, private tertiary facilities and emergency services.','High','[{"occupation":"Critical Care Nurse","description":"Manages critically ill patients in intensive care.","note":"Requires prior nursing registration plus post-basic certification."},{"occupation":"Emergency Unit Nurse","description":"Handles acute and trauma cases."}]'),
('Peri-Operative Nursing','Peri-operative nursing is post-basic training for nurses working in operating theatres before, during and after surgery.','You learn surgical procedures, sterile technique, theatre equipment, anaesthesia support and patient recovery, with extensive supervised theatre practice.','{"Surgical anatomy","Sterile technique and infection control","Theatre instrumentation","Anaesthesia support","Post-anaesthetic recovery","Theatre practicum"}','Theatre-trained nurses are needed wherever surgery is performed, making this a portable specialism with clear career progression into theatre management.','Teaching, regional, mission and private hospitals with surgical services.','High','[{"occupation":"Theatre Nurse","description":"Assists surgical teams in the operating theatre.","note":"Requires nursing registration plus post-basic theatre certification."},{"occupation":"Recovery Room Nurse","description":"Monitors patients immediately after surgery."}]'),
('Ophthalmic Nursing','Ophthalmic nursing is post-basic training in eye care and the nursing management of eye conditions.','You study eye anatomy, common eye diseases, vision testing, eye medications and assisting with eye surgery, with clinical practice in eye units.','{"Ocular anatomy","Common eye diseases","Vision assessment","Ophthalmic procedures","Eye surgery assistance"}','Eye care services are limited in many parts of Ghana, so trained ophthalmic nurses are in demand, especially in district and outreach eye services.','Hospital eye units, specialist eye centres, outreach and blindness-prevention programmes.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Ophthalmic Nurse","description":"Provides eye care and assists eye clinics.","note":"Requires nursing registration plus post-basic certification."},{"occupation":"Eye Screening Officer","description":"Runs community vision screening and outreach."}]'),
('ENT Nursing','ENT nursing is post-basic training in caring for patients with ear, nose and throat conditions.','You study ENT anatomy, hearing and airway problems, ENT procedures and post-operative care, with supervised practice in ENT clinics and theatres.','{"ENT anatomy","Hearing assessment","Airway and throat conditions","ENT procedures","Post-operative ENT care"}','It is a scarce specialism with steady referral demand in tertiary hospitals and a clear route to senior clinical roles.','Teaching and regional hospital ENT units and specialist private clinics.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"ENT Nurse","description":"Supports diagnosis and care of ear, nose and throat patients.","note":"Requires nursing registration plus post-basic certification."},{"occupation":"Audiology Support Officer","description":"Assists with hearing assessment services.","note":"Further audiology training may be required."}]'),
('Public Health Nursing','Public health nursing is post-basic training focused on population health, disease prevention and health systems.','You study epidemiology, health promotion, programme planning, environmental health and health data, applied to district and national health programmes.','{"Epidemiology","Health promotion","Programme planning and evaluation","Environmental health","Health data and surveillance"}','It moves nurses from individual care to shaping health programmes, opening supervisory and district-level roles and a natural bridge to postgraduate public health study.','District health directorates, Ghana Health Service programmes, NGOs and donor-funded health projects.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Public Health Nurse","description":"Leads preventive health programmes in a district.","note":"Requires nursing registration plus post-basic training."},{"occupation":"Disease Surveillance Officer","description":"Monitors and reports disease outbreaks."},{"occupation":"Health Programme Coordinator","description":"Plans and manages community health projects."}]'),
('Health Assistancy','Health assistancy trains support staff who help nurses and clinicians with everyday patient care.','You learn basic patient care, hygiene, vital signs, infection control, record keeping and how a health facility runs, with a strong practical placement component.','{"Basic patient care","Vital signs and observation","Infection prevention","Hygiene and nutrition support","Health records","Clinical placement"}','It is an accessible entry point into the health workforce with a shorter training period, and many holders later upgrade to nursing or midwifery qualifications.','Hospitals, clinics, CHPS compounds, elderly and home care services. Roles are supportive rather than independent clinical practice.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Health Care Assistant","description":"Supports nurses with day-to-day patient care.","note":"Scope of practice is limited and supervised."},{"occupation":"Ward Assistant","description":"Assists with ward routines and patient comfort."},{"occupation":"Home Care Aide","description":"Supports patients and elderly people at home."}]'),
('Medicine','Medicine trains you to diagnose and treat illness and to take clinical responsibility for patients as a doctor.','You begin with the basic sciences of the human body, then move into clinical rotations in medicine, surgery, paediatrics, obstetrics and other specialties, learning on the wards under supervision.','{"Anatomy and physiology","Biochemistry and pathology","Pharmacology","Internal medicine","Surgery","Paediatrics and obstetrics","Clinical clerkship"}','Medicine offers deep clinical skill, strong social standing, wide specialisation options and internationally portable training, though it demands a long commitment before full practice.','Teaching and regional hospitals, district health services, private hospitals, research and global health. Highly specialised path within health.','High','[{"occupation":"Medical Doctor","description":"Diagnoses and treats patients.","note":"Requires housemanship and Medical and Dental Council registration before independent practice."},{"occupation":"Medical Specialist","description":"Practises in a field such as surgery or paediatrics.","note":"Requires postgraduate residency training."},{"occupation":"Public Health Physician","description":"Leads health programmes and policy.","note":"Requires postgraduate public health training."},{"occupation":"Medical Researcher","description":"Conducts clinical or biomedical research."}]'),
('Pharmacy','Pharmacy trains you in medicines: how they work, how they are made and how to use them safely.','You study drug chemistry, how medicines act in the body, formulation, dispensing and patient counselling, with hospital and community pharmacy placements.','{"Pharmaceutical chemistry","Pharmacology","Pharmaceutics and formulation","Clinical pharmacy","Pharmacy law and ethics","Practicum"}','Pharmacists are needed in hospitals, retail, manufacturing and regulation, and the qualification supports entrepreneurship through community pharmacy ownership.','Hospital and community pharmacies, pharmaceutical manufacturers and importers, the Food and Drugs Authority, and health NGOs.','High','[{"occupation":"Pharmacist","description":"Dispenses medicines and advises on safe use.","note":"Requires internship and Pharmacy Council registration."},{"occupation":"Clinical Pharmacist","description":"Works with medical teams on medicine therapy.","note":"Often requires postgraduate training."},{"occupation":"Regulatory Affairs Officer","description":"Handles medicine registration and compliance."},{"occupation":"Pharmaceutical Sales Manager","description":"Manages product distribution and marketing."}]'),
('Health Sciences','Health sciences programmes train allied health professionals who diagnose, treat and rehabilitate patients alongside doctors and nurses.','You study human biology, disease processes and the specific techniques of your discipline, combined with supervised clinical placements.','{"Anatomy and physiology","Pathology","Discipline-specific clinical techniques","Patient assessment","Rehabilitation or diagnostic practice","Clinical placement"}','Allied health roles are in short supply in Ghana, offer defined professional licensing, and allow both hospital employment and private practice.','Teaching and regional hospitals, specialist clinics, private practice, sports and rehabilitation centres, and diagnostic services.','High','[{"occupation":"Allied Health Professional","description":"Practises in the specific discipline studied.","note":"Requires Allied Health Professions Council registration."},{"occupation":"Clinical Instructor","description":"Trains students in clinical settings.","note":"Usually requires experience and further study."},{"occupation":"Rehabilitation Officer","description":"Supports patient recovery programmes."}]'),
('Public Health','Public health focuses on keeping whole populations healthy through prevention, policy and health programmes.','You study epidemiology, biostatistics, environmental health, health policy and programme management, learning to use data to plan and evaluate health interventions.','{"Epidemiology","Biostatistics","Environmental health","Health policy and management","Health promotion","Research methods"}','It suits students who want health impact without clinical practice, and it is directly relevant to Ghana''s disease prevention, sanitation and health financing challenges, with strong NGO and donor demand.','Ghana Health Service, district assemblies, NGOs, donor-funded projects, research institutions and international agencies.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Public Health Officer","description":"Plans and runs preventive health programmes."},{"occupation":"Epidemiologist","description":"Investigates disease patterns and outbreaks.","note":"Senior roles usually require postgraduate study."},{"occupation":"Health Programme Manager","description":"Manages donor or government health projects."},{"occupation":"Environmental Health Officer","description":"Enforces sanitation and public health standards."}]'),
('Veterinary Science','Veterinary and animal health programmes train you to keep livestock and animals healthy and productive.','You study animal anatomy, nutrition, disease, treatment and farm management, with practical work on farms and in veterinary clinics.','{"Animal anatomy and physiology","Animal nutrition","Animal diseases and treatment","Livestock production","Public and zoonotic health","Field practicum"}','Livestock and poultry are central to Ghana''s food economy, and animal health specialists are scarce, with room for private practice, agribusiness and veterinary services work.','Veterinary Services Directorate, commercial farms, poultry and feed companies, agricultural NGOs and private clinics.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Veterinary Technician","description":"Treats and monitors animal health under supervision."},{"occupation":"Livestock Production Officer","description":"Advises farmers on breeding and husbandry."},{"occupation":"Veterinary Surgeon","description":"Practises veterinary medicine independently.","note":"Requires a full veterinary medicine degree and registration."}]'),
('Teacher Education','Teacher education prepares you to teach, manage a classroom and support children''s learning in Ghanaian schools.','You study how children learn, subject content, lesson planning, assessment and classroom management, and spend supervised terms teaching in real schools.','{"Educational psychology","Curriculum and subject methods","Lesson planning and assessment","Classroom management","Educational technology","Supported teaching in schools"}','Teaching offers dependable nationwide employment, a clear licensing route through the National Teaching Council, transferable communication and leadership skills, and pathways into school leadership, education policy or further study.','Public and private basic and secondary schools, education directorates, NGOs in education, curriculum and textbook work, and private tutoring.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Basic School Teacher","description":"Teaches at primary or junior high level.","note":"Requires National Teaching Council licensure."},{"occupation":"Subject Teacher","description":"Teaches a specialist subject in secondary school."},{"occupation":"Head Teacher","description":"Leads and manages a school.","note":"Requires experience and often further qualification."},{"occupation":"Education Officer","description":"Supports schools from a district education office."},{"occupation":"Curriculum Developer","description":"Designs learning materials and assessments."}]'),
('Education','Education programmes combine subject expertise with the skills to teach and lead learning.','You study your subject area alongside teaching methods, assessment, educational psychology and school practice, preparing you for classroom and wider education roles.','{"Subject specialisation","Teaching methods","Assessment and evaluation","Educational psychology","Educational technology","Teaching practice"}','It pairs a solid subject qualification with a professional route into teaching, giving flexibility to work in schools, training organisations, edtech or education administration.','Secondary and tertiary institutions, education NGOs, training providers, edtech companies and public education agencies.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Teacher","description":"Teaches the subject specialisation studied.","note":"Requires National Teaching Council licensure for public schools."},{"occupation":"Training Officer","description":"Designs and delivers staff training."},{"occupation":"Education Administrator","description":"Manages education programmes or institutions."},{"occupation":"Instructional Designer","description":"Creates digital and blended learning content."}]'),
('Technical Education','Technical education trains teachers and instructors for technical, vocational and practical subjects.','You learn a technical trade area in depth alongside teaching methods, workshop safety and competency-based assessment, with workshop and school practice.','{"Technical trade skills","Workshop practice and safety","Technical drawing","Teaching methods for TVET","Competency-based assessment","Teaching practice"}','Ghana is expanding TVET, so qualified technical instructors are in demand, and the trade skills themselves support contracting or self-employment alongside teaching.','Technical and vocational institutes, senior high technical schools, TVET agencies, industry training centres and construction or engineering firms.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Technical Instructor","description":"Teaches practical trade subjects."},{"occupation":"TVET Teacher","description":"Teaches in technical and vocational institutions.","note":"Requires teaching licensure for public institutions."},{"occupation":"Workshop Supervisor","description":"Runs training workshops and equipment."}]'),
('Engineering','Engineering trains you to design, build and maintain the systems, machines and structures people depend on.','You build a strong base in mathematics, physics and design, then specialise, using laboratories, drawing and modelling software, projects and industrial attachment to apply theory to real problems.','{"Engineering mathematics","Mechanics and materials","Design and CAD","Specialist engineering courses","Laboratory work","Project work and industrial attachment"}','Engineering skills are needed across Ghana''s energy, mining, construction, manufacturing and technology sectors, transfer well internationally, and support both employment and contracting or start-up work.','Construction and civil works, mining and oil and gas, power utilities, manufacturing, telecoms, consultancy firms and government agencies.','High','[{"occupation":"Engineer","description":"Designs and supervises technical systems in the field studied.","note":"Professional practice usually requires Ghana Institution of Engineering membership and licensure."},{"occupation":"Project Engineer","description":"Manages delivery of engineering projects."},{"occupation":"Maintenance Engineer","description":"Keeps plant and equipment running."},{"occupation":"Design Engineer","description":"Produces technical designs and specifications."},{"occupation":"Quality and Safety Engineer","description":"Ensures standards and safety compliance."}]'),
('Geomatic Engineering','Geomatics and surveying is about measuring land accurately and turning that data into maps and spatial information.','You study surveying instruments, land measurement, mapping, GPS, GIS and land law, with substantial fieldwork.','{"Land surveying","Geodesy and GPS","Cartography and mapping","Geographic Information Systems","Remote sensing","Land law and administration","Fieldwork"}','Land documentation, mining, construction and infrastructure projects in Ghana all depend on surveyors, and the skills support private consultancy work.','Lands Commission, survey and mapping firms, mining companies, construction and road projects, and GIS units.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Land Surveyor","description":"Measures and documents land boundaries.","note":"Licensed surveying work requires professional registration."},{"occupation":"GIS Analyst","description":"Builds and analyses spatial data and maps."},{"occupation":"Mine Surveyor","description":"Handles survey control on mining sites."}]'),
('Architecture','Architecture trains you to design buildings and spaces that are safe, functional and appealing.','You combine design studio work with building construction, structures, materials, environmental design and drawing software, presenting and defending your designs regularly.','{"Design studio","Building construction and materials","Architectural drawing and CAD","Structures","Environmental and climate-responsive design","History of architecture","Professional practice"}','It blends creativity with technical skill, is directly tied to Ghana''s growing property and construction market, and supports private practice once professionally qualified.','Architectural and design practices, real estate developers, construction firms, government works departments and self-employment.','High','[{"occupation":"Architectural Assistant","description":"Produces drawings and supports project design."},{"occupation":"Architect","description":"Leads building design projects.","note":"Requires further professional qualification and registration with the Architects Registration Council."},{"occupation":"Interior Designer","description":"Designs functional and attractive interiors."},{"occupation":"Project Coordinator","description":"Coordinates design and construction delivery."}]'),
('Construction','Construction and building technology trains you to plan, cost and manage the physical delivery of buildings.','You study construction methods, materials, structures, site management, estimating and safety, with site visits and practical attachment.','{"Construction technology","Building materials","Structural principles","Quantity estimating and costing","Site and project management","Health and safety"}','Ghana''s housing and infrastructure demand keeps construction active, and the skills support contracting, project management or self-employment.','Contractors, real estate developers, consultancy firms, public works departments and materials suppliers.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Site Supervisor","description":"Manages day-to-day construction work."},{"occupation":"Quantity Surveyor","description":"Prices and controls project costs.","note":"Professional practice usually requires further qualification and registration."},{"occupation":"Building Technologist","description":"Applies construction technology on projects."},{"occupation":"Contracts Officer","description":"Handles procurement and contract administration."}]'),
('Computer Science','Computer science focuses on programming, algorithms, software development, data, artificial intelligence and computer systems.','You learn how to write and structure programs, how computers and networks work, how data is stored and searched, and how to build reliable software. Expect a mix of mathematics, coding assignments and team projects.','{"Programming","Data structures and algorithms","Databases","Software engineering","Computer networks","Operating systems","Artificial intelligence"}','Software skills are portable, pay reasonably in Ghana''s fintech and telecom sectors, allow remote work for foreign employers, support freelancing and start-ups, and lead into fast-growing areas like data and AI.','Fintech and mobile money companies, telecoms, banks, software houses, government digitalisation projects, and remote work for international employers. Very broad career paths.','High','[{"occupation":"Software Developer","description":"Builds and maintains applications and systems."},{"occupation":"Data Analyst","description":"Turns data into insight and reporting."},{"occupation":"Systems Analyst","description":"Improves how business systems and processes work."},{"occupation":"Cybersecurity Analyst","description":"Protects systems from attack.","note":"Employers often expect security certification."},{"occupation":"Database Administrator","description":"Designs and maintains databases."},{"occupation":"Cloud Engineer","description":"Runs cloud infrastructure.","note":"Cloud provider certification is commonly expected."}]'),
('Information Technology','Information technology is about running, securing and supporting the systems and networks that organisations depend on.','You study networks, systems administration, databases, web technologies, support and IT project work, with hands-on labs and attachment.','{"Computer networks","Systems administration","Databases","Web and application support","IT security basics","IT project management"}','IT roles exist in almost every organisation in Ghana, entry is possible with practical skills and certifications, and the field allows steady progression into networking, security or systems management.','Banks, telecoms, government agencies, schools, NGOs and IT service providers. Broad demand across sectors.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"IT Support Officer","description":"Keeps users, devices and systems working."},{"occupation":"Network Administrator","description":"Runs and secures organisational networks.","note":"Vendor certification such as CCNA is often expected."},{"occupation":"Systems Administrator","description":"Manages servers and business systems."},{"occupation":"Web Developer","description":"Builds and maintains websites and web apps."}]'),
('Cybersecurity','Cybersecurity trains you to protect computer systems, networks and data from attack and misuse.','You learn networking and systems fundamentals, then attack and defence techniques, cryptography, digital forensics, risk management and security law, with practical lab work.','{"Networking and systems","Cryptography","Ethical hacking and penetration testing","Digital forensics","Security operations and monitoring","Risk, governance and cyber law"}','Ghana''s Cybersecurity Act and rapid digital banking growth have created real demand for security skills, roles are hard to fill, and the field supports consulting and international remote work.','Banks and fintechs, telecoms, the Cyber Security Authority, consulting firms, and security operations teams.','High','[{"occupation":"Cybersecurity Analyst","description":"Monitors and defends systems against threats.","note":"Certifications such as Security+ or CEH are commonly expected."},{"occupation":"Penetration Tester","description":"Tests systems by attempting controlled attacks.","note":"Requires certification and authorised engagement."},{"occupation":"Security Engineer","description":"Builds and hardens secure infrastructure."},{"occupation":"Digital Forensics Analyst","description":"Investigates incidents and cybercrime."}]'),
('Data Science','Data science is about using data, statistics and programming to answer questions and support decisions.','You combine statistics and mathematics with programming, data cleaning, visualisation, databases and machine learning, working on real datasets in projects.','{"Statistics and probability","Programming for data","Data wrangling and databases","Data visualisation","Machine learning","Applied data projects"}','Banks, telecoms and development organisations in Ghana increasingly rely on data, the skills combine well with any sector, and analytics work is one of the more accessible routes into international remote employment.','Banks, insurance, telecoms, fintech, research institutes, NGOs and international organisations.','High','[{"occupation":"Data Analyst","description":"Analyses data and builds reports and dashboards."},{"occupation":"Data Scientist","description":"Builds predictive models from data."},{"occupation":"Business Intelligence Analyst","description":"Turns business data into decision tools."},{"occupation":"Machine Learning Engineer","description":"Puts models into production systems.","note":"Usually requires strong software engineering skills."}]'),
('Artificial Intelligence','Artificial intelligence focuses on building systems that learn from data and perform tasks that normally need human intelligence.','You study mathematics, programming, machine learning, neural networks, natural language and computer vision, plus the ethics of automated decisions, with substantial project work.','{"Mathematics for AI","Programming","Machine learning","Deep learning and neural networks","Natural language processing","Computer vision","AI ethics"}','AI skills are scarce globally and in Ghana, they combine well with health, agriculture and finance problems locally, and they open both research routes and high-value remote work.','Fintech, telecoms, research institutions, health and agriculture technology projects, and international remote roles.','High','[{"occupation":"Machine Learning Engineer","description":"Builds and deploys learning systems."},{"occupation":"AI Research Assistant","description":"Supports applied AI research.","note":"Research roles often expect postgraduate study."},{"occupation":"Data Scientist","description":"Applies models to business and social problems."},{"occupation":"Computer Vision Engineer","description":"Builds systems that interpret images and video."}]'),
('Applied Sciences','Applied science programmes take core science and apply it to industry, laboratories and product development.','You study your science discipline in depth with heavy laboratory work, analysis techniques, quality control and research methods, plus industrial attachment.','{"Core science theory","Laboratory techniques","Instrumentation and analysis","Quality control","Research methods","Industrial attachment"}','Laboratory and quality skills are needed by Ghana''s mining, food, water, pharmaceutical and regulatory sectors, and the training is a strong base for postgraduate study or research careers.','Mining and processing companies, food and beverage manufacturers, water and environmental agencies, regulatory bodies, hospitals and research institutes.','High','[{"occupation":"Laboratory Analyst","description":"Runs tests and analyses samples."},{"occupation":"Quality Control Officer","description":"Ensures products meet standards."},{"occupation":"Research Assistant","description":"Supports scientific research projects."},{"occupation":"Production Supervisor","description":"Oversees technical production processes."}]'),
('Environment','Environmental and natural resource programmes study how to manage land, water, forests and ecosystems sustainably.','You learn ecology, resource management, environmental impact assessment, climate issues, GIS and policy, with fieldwork and case studies.','{"Ecology","Natural resource management","Environmental impact assessment","Climate change and adaptation","GIS and remote sensing","Environmental policy and law","Fieldwork"}','Mining, oil and gas, and donor projects in Ghana all require environmental assessment and compliance work, and climate adaptation funding continues to expand the field.','Environmental Protection Agency, mining and energy companies, forestry and water agencies, consultancies and environmental NGOs.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Environmental Officer","description":"Monitors compliance and environmental performance."},{"occupation":"Environmental Consultant","description":"Prepares impact assessments and management plans."},{"occupation":"Natural Resource Manager","description":"Manages forests, land or water resources."},{"occupation":"Sustainability Officer","description":"Runs corporate environmental programmes."}]'),
('Agriculture','Agriculture programmes teach how food and agricultural products are produced, processed and sold profitably.','You study crop and animal production, soils, pests, farm management, agribusiness and value chains, with practical farm work and attachment.','{"Crop production","Animal production","Soil science","Crop protection","Agribusiness and marketing","Post-harvest handling","Farm practicum"}','Agriculture is one of Ghana''s largest employers and government priorities, the skills directly support running your own farm or agribusiness, and value-chain and agritech roles are expanding.','Agribusiness firms, input and seed companies, food processors, Ministry of Food and Agriculture, banks with agri portfolios, NGOs and self-employment.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Agricultural Extension Officer","description":"Advises farmers on better production methods."},{"occupation":"Farm Manager","description":"Runs commercial crop or livestock operations."},{"occupation":"Agribusiness Officer","description":"Handles agricultural inputs, sales and value chains."},{"occupation":"Agricultural Research Assistant","description":"Supports crop and livestock research."}]'),
('Business','Business programmes teach how organisations are run, financed, marketed and grown.','You study management, marketing, accounting, economics, operations, human resources and business law, with case studies, group projects and internships.','{"Principles of management","Marketing","Accounting and finance basics","Economics","Operations and supply chain","Human resource management","Business law and ethics"}','Business skills apply to every sector, make self-employment realistic, are valued by Ghana''s banking, telecom, retail and NGO employers, and combine well with professional certifications for faster progression.','Banks and insurance, telecoms, FMCG and retail, logistics, NGOs, consulting and family businesses. One of the broadest career paths available.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Business Development Officer","description":"Wins new clients and grows revenue."},{"occupation":"Marketing Officer","description":"Plans campaigns and manages brands."},{"occupation":"Operations Officer","description":"Keeps day-to-day business processes running."},{"occupation":"Human Resource Officer","description":"Handles recruitment and staff management.","note":"Professional HR certification helps for senior roles."},{"occupation":"Entrepreneur","description":"Starts and runs a business."}]'),
('Accounting','Accounting is about recording, reporting and interpreting the financial position of an organisation.','You study financial and management accounting, auditing, taxation, business law and accounting software, with practice-based assignments and internships.','{"Financial accounting","Management accounting","Auditing","Taxation","Business law","Accounting information systems"}','Every organisation needs accounting, the degree maps directly onto ICAG and ACCA professional exams, and qualified accountants have some of the clearest promotion ladders and private-practice options in Ghana.','Audit and accounting firms, banks, Ghana Revenue Authority, public sector finance offices, NGOs and private companies.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Accounts Officer","description":"Maintains records and prepares financial reports."},{"occupation":"Auditor","description":"Examines financial records for accuracy.","note":"Practising as a chartered auditor requires ICAG or ACCA qualification."},{"occupation":"Tax Officer","description":"Handles tax compliance and advice."},{"occupation":"Financial Analyst","description":"Analyses performance to guide decisions."}]'),
('Finance','Finance is about managing money, investment and risk for people, companies and institutions.','You study financial markets, banking, corporate finance, investment analysis, risk management and financial modelling, using real market data in assignments.','{"Corporate finance","Financial markets and institutions","Investment analysis","Risk management","Financial modelling","Banking operations"}','Ghana''s banking, insurance, pensions and capital markets need finance skills, the field pays comparatively well, and it links to global certifications such as ACCA and CFA for international mobility.','Banks, insurance companies, pension and investment firms, the Bank of Ghana and regulators, fintechs and corporate finance departments.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Banking Officer","description":"Handles credit, operations or relationship management."},{"occupation":"Financial Analyst","description":"Evaluates investments and company performance."},{"occupation":"Credit Risk Analyst","description":"Assesses lending risk."},{"occupation":"Investment Adviser","description":"Advises clients on investments.","note":"Requires licensing by the Securities and Exchange Commission."}]'),
('Law','Law trains you to understand legal rules, argue a case and advise people and organisations on their rights and obligations.','You study constitutional, criminal, contract, land, family and commercial law, plus legal research and writing, with heavy reading, case analysis and mooting.','{"Constitutional law","Criminal law","Law of contract","Land law","Company and commercial law","Legal research and writing","Mooting and advocacy"}','Law develops analysis and argument skills valued far beyond the courtroom, supports careers in business, policy and compliance, and leads to private practice once professional training is completed.','Law firms, corporate legal and compliance departments, banks, government ministries, the judicial service, NGOs and regulators.','High','[{"occupation":"Legal Officer","description":"Advises an organisation on legal matters."},{"occupation":"Lawyer","description":"Represents and advises clients.","note":"Requires the Ghana School of Law professional course and call to the Bar."},{"occupation":"Compliance Officer","description":"Ensures the organisation follows laws and regulations."},{"occupation":"Legal Researcher","description":"Researches law and policy issues."}]'),
('Public Administration','Public administration studies how government and public organisations are run and how policy is delivered.','You study governance, public policy, public finance, human resource management, administrative law and ethics, with case studies of real institutions.','{"Public policy","Governance and administration","Public financial management","Administrative law","Human resource management","Local government","Ethics and accountability"}','It is a direct route into Ghana''s public service, district assemblies and development organisations, and the skills also transfer to project management and NGO administration.','Ministries, departments and agencies, district assemblies, state corporations, NGOs and donor-funded programmes.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Administrative Officer","description":"Runs administration in a public institution."},{"occupation":"Policy Analyst","description":"Researches and advises on public policy."},{"occupation":"Local Government Officer","description":"Supports district-level administration and services."},{"occupation":"Programme Officer","description":"Coordinates public or donor-funded programmes."}]'),
('Development','Development studies looks at why poverty and inequality persist and what actually works to reduce them.','You study development theory, economics, social policy, project planning, monitoring and evaluation and research methods, often with fieldwork in communities.','{"Development theory","Development economics","Social policy","Project planning and management","Monitoring and evaluation","Research methods","Fieldwork"}','It is well suited to Ghana''s large NGO and donor sector, builds practical project and evaluation skills employers ask for, and pairs well with postgraduate study in policy or economics.','NGOs, donor agencies, district assemblies, research institutes, social enterprises and CSR departments.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Project Officer","description":"Delivers development projects on the ground."},{"occupation":"Monitoring and Evaluation Officer","description":"Measures whether programmes work."},{"occupation":"Community Development Officer","description":"Works with communities on local development."},{"occupation":"Research Assistant","description":"Supports social and policy research."}]'),
('Peace and Security','Peace and security programmes study conflict, its causes and how peace and security are maintained.','You study conflict analysis, mediation, security studies, international relations, governance and research methods, using real case studies from Ghana and the region.','{"Conflict analysis","Peacebuilding and mediation","Security studies","International relations","Governance and human rights","Research methods"}','Chieftaincy, land and regional security issues make this directly relevant to Ghana and the wider Sahel, and it supports careers in security agencies, regional bodies and peacebuilding organisations.','Security services, ECOWAS and regional institutions, international organisations, think tanks, NGOs and government ministries.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Peacebuilding Officer","description":"Runs conflict prevention and mediation programmes."},{"occupation":"Security Analyst","description":"Assesses security risks and trends."},{"occupation":"Policy Researcher","description":"Researches peace, governance and security policy."}]'),
('Psychology','Psychology is the study of how people think, feel and behave, and how to support mental wellbeing.','You study human development, cognition, social behaviour, abnormal psychology, research methods and statistics, with practical studies and projects.','{"Developmental psychology","Cognitive psychology","Social psychology","Abnormal psychology","Research methods and statistics","Counselling foundations"}','Mental health and workplace wellbeing are gaining attention in Ghana, the degree builds strong research and people skills useful in HR, education and health, and it leads into clinical or organisational specialisation with further study.','Schools, hospitals and clinics, human resource departments, NGOs, research organisations and counselling services.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Counsellor","description":"Supports clients with personal and emotional issues.","note":"Professional counselling usually requires further training and registration."},{"occupation":"Human Resource Officer","description":"Applies behavioural insight to workplace management."},{"occupation":"Research Assistant","description":"Supports psychological and social research."},{"occupation":"Clinical Psychologist","description":"Assesses and treats mental health conditions.","note":"Requires postgraduate clinical training and registration."}]'),
('Languages','Language and translation programmes build advanced skill in a language and the ability to move meaning accurately between languages.','You study grammar, comprehension, writing, interpreting, translation techniques, terminology and culture, with substantial practice work.','{"Advanced language study","Translation techniques","Interpreting practice","Terminology and specialised texts","Linguistics","Culture and communication"}','Ghana''s position among francophone neighbours, plus ECOWAS and international organisations, creates ongoing demand for translators and interpreters, and the skill supports well-paid freelance work.','Government ministries, embassies, ECOWAS and international organisations, media, translation agencies and freelance work.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Translator","description":"Translates documents between languages."},{"occupation":"Interpreter","description":"Interprets speech at meetings and conferences.","note":"Conference interpreting usually requires specialist training."},{"occupation":"Language Teacher","description":"Teaches the language in schools or institutes."},{"occupation":"Communications Officer","description":"Handles multilingual communication for organisations."}]'),
('Theology','Theology and divinity study religious texts, belief, ethics and the practice of ministry.','You study scripture, church history, doctrine, ethics, pastoral care, preaching and counselling, often with supervised ministry placement.','{"Biblical studies","Church history","Systematic theology","Ethics","Pastoral care and counselling","Homiletics","Ministry placement"}','Faith institutions are major employers and social actors in Ghana, and the training also develops counselling, teaching, leadership and community organising skills used in NGOs and schools.','Churches and faith-based organisations, mission schools, chaplaincy services, faith-based NGOs and counselling ministries.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Pastor or Minister","description":"Leads a congregation and pastoral work.","note":"Ordination requirements are set by each denomination."},{"occupation":"Chaplain","description":"Provides spiritual care in schools, hospitals or services."},{"occupation":"Religious Studies Teacher","description":"Teaches religious and moral education."},{"occupation":"Faith-Based Programme Officer","description":"Runs community and development programmes."}]'),
('Hospitality','Hospitality management prepares you to run hotels, restaurants, events and tourism services.','You study front office and accommodation operations, food and beverage, customer service, hospitality accounting, marketing and events, with industrial attachment in hotels.','{"Front office operations","Food and beverage management","Housekeeping and accommodation","Customer service","Hospitality accounting and cost control","Events and tourism marketing","Industrial attachment"}','Tourism and events are growth areas in Ghana, the skills are highly practical and portable internationally, and small hospitality businesses can be started with modest capital.','Hotels and resorts, restaurants and catering companies, event management firms, airlines and travel companies, and self-employment.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Hotel Operations Officer","description":"Runs front office or accommodation services."},{"occupation":"Food and Beverage Supervisor","description":"Manages restaurant and catering operations."},{"occupation":"Events Coordinator","description":"Plans and delivers events."},{"occupation":"Tourism Officer","description":"Promotes and manages tourism services."}]'),
('Film and Television','Film and television training teaches you to plan, shoot, direct and edit visual stories.','You study scriptwriting, camera and lighting, sound, directing, editing and production management, learning mainly by making films and TV pieces.','{"Scriptwriting","Cinematography and lighting","Sound recording","Directing","Editing and post-production","Production management"}','Ghana''s film, advertising and streaming content market is expanding, freelance and commercial work is available early, and the skills carry into digital content, corporate media and international co-productions.','Production houses, television stations, advertising agencies, corporate communications, streaming and digital content, and freelance work.','Moderate','[{"occupation":"Video Editor","description":"Assembles and finishes filmed material."},{"occupation":"Cinematographer","description":"Plans and shoots visual images."},{"occupation":"Producer","description":"Organises budgets, crew and delivery of productions."},{"occupation":"Content Creator","description":"Produces digital video for brands and platforms."}]'),
('General','This programme prepares you with specialist knowledge and practical skills in its field of study.','You combine theory with practical coursework, projects and, where relevant, supervised placement or attachment. Check the institution''s official programme page for the exact course structure.','{"Core theory in the discipline","Practical coursework","Research or project work"}','It provides a recognised, accredited qualification in a defined field, with progression into employment or further study. Review the official programme page and speak to the institution to confirm the specific advantages.','Employment depends on the specific discipline and institution. Check the institution''s official programme page and the current labour market before deciding.','Moderate','[]');
